# Line endings. Every text file is stored LF in the repository and checked out LF on
# every platform, overriding Git for Windows' default `core.autocrlf=true`.
#
# This is not a style preference. The model inputs are read as bytes by the suites --
# krlib's `test_the_csvs_are_utf8_without_a_bom` asserts the CSVs carry no BOM and no
# CRLF, because a BOM lands in the first column name and the encoding is load-bearing
# where the provenance columns are Korean. Without the rule below, a Windows checkout
# rewrites all 333 input CSVs to CRLF and that test fails on Windows alone, against
# files that are LF in the repository. Every tracked file here is text, so there is
# nothing to exclude.
* text=auto eol=lf

# `cmd.exe` is the one consumer that wants CRLF.
*.bat text eol=crlf
